1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
CEDAS has entered Customs and the next step is to prepare a Mexican Customs entry.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In Mexico we call them Pedimentos.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
It's really an appraisal sheet. It's a breakdown of the sheet.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Usually the same information.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
That's right.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
But here you give them all the information.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
For example, let me see if I've got one right here.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
You give them all the information on...

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
on what the invoice contains.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,000
There's one.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
On what the invoice contains.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
What the material is.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,000
It's all physically here.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
For example, this is some bottling equipment going over there.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
And on this appraisal sheet you tell them who it's for.

16
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Who made the invoice out of the States.

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
This came from St. Louis, Missouri.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
How much the freight was.

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
And on the reverse of this thing, you put that everything has to be marked.

20
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
In other words, this identification number is that traffic number I spoke to you a little while ago.

21
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Number of boxes, what they contain, the tariff duty, the tariff number, the ad valorem rate, and what the actual duties would be paid.

22
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
For example, here it would be 996 pesos and 73 cents.

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
As you can see, this is a form that has already been approved by the appraiser.

24
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
These appraisers are called vistas.

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
It's very different from the vistas we have nowadays.

